  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India, DBIE: variables published bank and bank group-wise (report 1221), and the data tables of the Primary (Urban) Co-operative Banks' Outlook (reports 772, 784 to 789, 795 to 800), both gated behind a prompt on DBIE and read through the Reserve Bank Innovation Hub's data service; the Outlook's typed tables (771, 773 to 777, 810 to 812) and the financial-institutions tables (382 to 398, 801, 873, 1372), read from India Atlas's archived copy of DBIE. Branches, offices and NBFC credit are the credit guide's bundles. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={N["prov-vintage"]}></b>.</p>
        <p>Checked by hand: State Bank of India's gross NPAs for March 2025, ₹76,880 crore and 1.82%, equal SBI's audited results; insured deposits for March 2025, ₹100.12 lakh crore, equal DICGC's published figure.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Amounts converted to ₹ crore (₹ lakh crore on the charts). Banks named as the RBI names them; four renamed banks joined, mergers never joined. Identities checked on every bank and quarter: deposits, assets and liabilities add up, gross NPAs equal their three classes, the printed NPA ratio equals NPAs over advances, and the bank groups add to all banks. Shares of deposits and advances are computed by India Atlas and labelled. Nothing is estimated.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Report 1221 is not revised once printed; the annual tables sometimes revise a March figure, and this guide keeps 1221's. The Outlook's latest March is provisional and is replaced by the next edition's figure. The infrastructure list was renumbered in June 2022 (two rulers, never joined). Bank groups change as the RBI moves banks between them.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0 (October 2026), from RBI data to {PH.long} (banks) and {PU.long} (urban co-operative banks). Revised each quarter when the RBI publishes the next bank-wise return.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
